          body: T('先手算：用 ψ = (ζ³/π) e^{−ζ(r₁+r₂)}，动能给 ζ²，核吸引给 −4ζ，电子排斥给 5ζ/8，合起来 E(ζ) = ζ² − 27ζ/8，极小在 ζ = 27/16。再用 PySCF 对 He 做 HF（cc-pVQZ 约 −2.8615 E_h）和 FCI，依次比较：单参数变分、HF 极限、FCI。三个数字之间的两段差距，分别是“轨道形状的自由度”和“电子关联”。',
            'First by hand: with ψ = (ζ³/π) e^{−ζ(r₁+r₂)}, the kinetic energy gives ζ², nuclear attraction −4ζ and electron repulsion 5ζ/8, so E(ζ) = ζ² − 27ζ/8 with its minimum at ζ = 27/16. Then run HF (cc-pVQZ, about −2.8615 E_h) and FCI on He with PySCF and compare: one-parameter variation, the HF limit, FCI. The two gaps between the three numbers are "freedom in the orbital shape" and "electron correlation".'),
